  "dimensions": [
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_1fee00ed",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts King Charles III with overlaid text that reads: 'when you've waited 40 years to be king, but your mother refuses to die.' This meme uses a juxtaposition of the king's solemn expression and the text to imply frustration or impatience with the Queen's prolonged life, which is framed as an obstacle to his ascension. While not explicitly targeting a protected group with hate, the meme is harmful because it trivializes the gravity of royal succession, the personal grief of the monarch, and the cultural significance of the monarchy. It also potentially undermines the dignity of the late Queen Elizabeth II by suggesting her continued life was an inconvenience to her son. The meme's intent is to provoke humor through a cynical, almost sarcastic commentary on royal protocol and personal timing, which can be seen as disrespectful and insensitive to the institution and its history. The tone is mocking and could be perceived as undermining the legitimacy or emotional weight of the monarchy, thus carrying potential harm to public perception and respect for the institution.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_7f6431e8"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
