      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_b1aea190",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "royal_succession",
      "label": "Royal Succession",
      "description": "The process by which a monarch inherits the throne, governed by laws and traditions such as the Act of Settlement 1701 and the Succession to the Crown Act 2013. In the UK, the monarch is succeeded by their eldest child, and the line of succession is strictly defined. This background knowledge is necessary to understand why Charles III waited 40 years to become king — because he was the heir apparent to Queen Elizabeth II, who reigned for 70 years and died in 2022, making Charles the next in line.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_7f6431e8"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_a55a8975",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "queen_elizabeth_ii",
      "label": "Queen Elizabeth II",
      "description": "The monarch of the United Kingdom and other Commonwealth realms from 1952 until her death in 2022. She was the mother of King Charles III and reigned for 70 years. Her prolonged life, as referenced in the meme, is the central obstacle to Charles’s ascension, which is why the meme implies frustration. This knowledge is essential to understand the meme’s context — Charles waited 40 years for his mother to die so he could become king.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_7f6431e8"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_b2534948",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "monarchy",
      "label": "The British Monarchy",
      "description": "A constitutional monarchy with a long history and deep cultural significance in the UK and Commonwealth. The institution is characterized by ceremonial duties, historical continuity, and public reverence. The meme’s humor and potential harm stem from its implication that the monarchy’s protocol is a source of personal frustration, which is disrespectful to the institution’s gravity and the personal grief of the monarch. Understanding the cultural weight of the monarchy is necessary to interpret the meme’s tone and intent.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_7f6431e8"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_14c1bcda",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "impatience_stereotype",
      "label": "Impatience Stereotype",
      "description": "A social stereotype that portrays individuals as frustrated or annoyed when things take longer than expected. The meme uses this stereotype to imply that King Charles III is impatient with his mother’s prolonged life, which is framed as an obstacle to his ascension. This stereotype is not directly visible in the image but is essential to understand the meme’s humorous and cynical tone.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_7f6431e8"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_e38bcf87",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "grief_and_loss",
      "label": "Grief and Loss",
      "description": "The emotional response to the death of a loved one. The meme trivializes the personal grief of King Charles III, who lost his mother, Queen Elizabeth II, in 2022. The humor in the meme is derived from mocking the idea that grief is an inconvenience, which is insensitive to the emotional weight of royal succession and the personal loss experienced by the monarch. Understanding grief is necessary to interpret the meme’s potential harm.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_7f6431e8"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_81e44438",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "cynical_humor",
      "label": "Cynical Humor",
      "description": "A style of humor that is sarcastic, mocking, or pessimistic, often used to critique or ridicule a situation. The meme uses cynical humor to comment on royal protocol and personal timing, implying that Charles’s wait for his mother’s death is an inconvenience. This style of humor is not visible in the image but is essential to understand the meme’s intent and tone.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
